  30:  *	o)  [RESOLVED as #389: big-endian LDRD/STRD were three defects deep --
  31:  *	    a word-pair inversion on both sides, a carry-corrupting data[1]<<6
  32:  *	    term, and a copy-pasted LE branch. Both sides now assemble TWO
  33:  *	    independent 32-bit words per DDI 0100I A4.1.26/A4.1.102.]
  34:  *
  35:  *	o)  "Base Updated Abort Model", which updates the base register
  36:  *	    even if the memory access failed.
  37:  *
  38:  *	o)  Some ARM implementations use pc+8, some use pc+12 for stores?
  39:  *	    [ANSWERED as #390: yes, and A2-9 (ddi0100i.txt:1637-1641) makes it an
  40:  *	    IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED choice for the STORED VALUE when Rd is R15 --
  41:  *	    but it REQUIRES one choice to be used for every ARM STR and STM that
  42:  *	    stores R15.  This fork uses +12, here and in the STM path, and those
  43:  *	    two sites must change together or not at all.  Note this latitude
  44:  *	    covers only the stored VALUE: the BASE, when R15 is Rn, is defined as
  45:  *	    instruction+8 with no choice about it.  Conflating the two is what
  46:  *	    #390 fixed.]
  47:  *
  48:  *	o)  All load/store variants with the PC register are not really
  49:  *	    valid. (E.g. a byte load into the PC register. What should that
  50:  *	    accomplish?)
  51:  *
  52:  *	o)  Perhaps an optimization for the case when offset = 0, because
  53:  *	    that's quite common, and also when the Reg expression is just
  54:  *	    a simple, non-rotated register (0..14).
  55:  */
